{"id": "EUVD-2026-93121", "enisaUuid": "8b076f41-2e1e-354f-a890-753dd37e3af5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libipw: reject TKIP frames without a full MIC\n\nlibipw_michael_mic_verify() assumes that an skb contains an eight-byte\nMichael MIC. A short TKIP frame makes the unsigned payload length wrap,\ncausing michael_mic() to read past the skb.\n\nCheck that the MIC is present before verifying it, and use the existing\nMICHAEL_MIC_LEN constant for all MIC lengths in the verifier.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f448b267968d0ee985e5927c868c8f858169ab34", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a7fb67364817710c96785ff86b71a2711ee92cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac7c08626f67844336086cf563f417566b76f0d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb7ae8910cc886885aea95abb7c2e578a2341646", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06f42accaf3c6aecab1dcc57f68dde6c06c8b380"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98193", "GHSA-8rh9-27vf-9cwr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ad67dd2-e194-38ea-869e-63730b6babd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.14"}, {"id": "146343a5-727f-3a5a-a2e8-bb1b206274a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b453872c35cfcbdbf5a794737817f7d4e7b1b579 <f448b267968d0ee985e5927c868c8f858169ab34"}, {"id": "270a20de-50e5-3eb3-9138-d7f0c9ebfefe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b453872c35cfcbdbf5a794737817f7d4e7b1b579 <06f42accaf3c6aecab1dcc57f68dde6c06c8b380"}, {"id": "2c59aefa-1f35-3e6a-a363-e6895b96073d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "2eeb61fd-0c4e-3bd1-848a-2adc42a7ad23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"i